cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this lab or its detection rules in research or teaching, please
  cite it as below.
title: >-
  mcp-objauthz-lab: a vulnerable-by-design MCP server and Semgrep ruleset for
  object-level authorization flaws
abstract: >-
  A self-hostable synthetic Model Context Protocol server carrying thirteen planted
  object-level authorization flaws (BOLA/IDOR, CWE-639 and CWE-862), one per
  challenge, together with a Semgrep ruleset that detects the same code shapes
  in real MCP server source. The ruleset covers JavaScript and TypeScript;
  eleven of its rules target Python, and eight further languages have
  rules of their own. It is distributed as a GitHub Action and uploads SARIF
  findings to a repository's security tab.
type: software
